# deploy: nightly version cut + deploy. `version cut` tags origin/main's tip
# as vYYYY.MM.DD (the night's JARVIS version); `version deploy` deploys it —
# pull the pinned checkout forward (or honor a `gazette version switch`
# rollback pin) and re-run the post-deploy steps (uv sync, link-clis,
# install-cron) so venv/CLIs/crontab always match the deployed tree. Merges
# happen hourly, but the BOX changes only here — this is the version boundary.
# Rollback: gazette version switch v<date>; resume: gazette version switch latest.
10 4 * * * { /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/gazette version cut && /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/gazette version deploy; } >> /home/daniel/.claude/logs/deploy.log 2>&1

# jarvis-memory: nightly auto-snapshot commit+push. ~/jarvis-memory is its
# own private repo (dtch1997/jarvis-memory, spun back out of the monorepo
# 2026-08-20 — issues #46/#47): memory is state, version rollback never
# touches it, and `git add -A` here is scoped by the repo boundary.
# RESUMED 2026-09-16 (protective; push auth verified on this box).
41 3 * * * cd /home/daniel/jarvis-memory && git add -A && git commit -qm "auto-snapshot $(date +\%F)" >/dev/null 2>&1; git push -q >> /home/daniel/.claude/logs/memory-backup.log 2>&1

# gazette: hourly merge-on-green sweep (consumer-mode PR flow — see CLAUDE.md
# "PR flow"; auto merges on green within the hour, requires-approval never);
# morning edition at 08:05 (spooled + flare; folds in the desk digest, so
# there is no separate desk→flare cron — see docs/morning-routine.md)
29 * * * * /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/gazette sweep >> /home/daniel/.claude/logs/gazette.log 2>&1
5 8 * * * /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/gazette notes --flare >> /home/daniel/.claude/logs/gazette.log 2>&1

# desk: hourly inbox sync (new blocked items still flare immediately)
7 * * * * /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/desk sync >> /home/daniel/.claude/logs/desk.log 2>&1

# threads: daily activity refresh — summarize new sessions, re-weave onto the
# registry (weave also refreshes the Obsidian vault). scan needs the API key
# from ~/.env; hitting the per-run call cap self-reports via flare.
#PAUSED# 19 7 * * * set -a; . /home/daniel/.env; set +a; /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/threads scan && /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/threads weave >> /home/daniel/.claude/logs/threads.log 2>&1

# threads: daily auto-wrapup backstop (docs/auto-wrapup.md) — runs after
# scan && weave, which refresh the activity data it reads. Deterministic and
# offline (zero model calls): it classifies every stale thread into terminal /
# blocked / A1 (abandoned, mechanically recoverable) / A2 (abandoned with a
# dirty worktree — never auto-touched) / B (parked and forgotten), writes
# ~/.threads/sweep/<date>.md, and sends one info flare on non-idle days.
# Report mode: dispatching wrap-up workers is config-gated ([sweep] mode in
# ~/.threads/config.toml) and stays OFF until Daniel flips it. Sources ~/.env
# and uses the PATH above for `gh` (PR state) and `git`.
#PAUSED# 49 7 * * * set -a; . /home/daniel/.env; set +a; /home/daniel/jarvis/.venv/bin/threads sweep >> /home/daniel/.claude/logs/threads.log 2>&1

